No Python upstream or signature JS. This is an original TypeScript adapter for the official API.

Verified with an authenticated account (read-only; no real data kept in repository):
- POST /member/profile: empty form, response data.id / username / memberCount
- POST /torrent/search: JSON {mode,categories,keyword,pageNumber,pageSize}; response data {pageNumber,pageSize,total,totalPages,data[]}
- POST /torrent/detail: form {id}; response is a torrent object
- POST /torrent/categoryList: empty form; response data.list[] contains id/nameChs/nameCht/nameEng/parent

Download request contract cross-checked against maintained client implementations; real download verified 2026-11-03:
- POST /torrent/genDlToken: form {id}; response data is a temporary download URL
- GET the returned HTTPS M-Team URL without forwarding x-api-key, save .torrent only
- No BT client integration, Tracker announce, upload, or automatic seeding

Additional primary implementation references for protocol cross-checks (no source copied):
- https://github.com/Jackett/Jackett/blob/master/src/Jackett.Common/Indexers/Definitions/MTeamTp.cs (blob 0323ec0d976e44d13f39a08d354f3d6ed7f33f81)
- https://github.com/pt-plugins/PT-depiler/blob/master/src/packages/site/definitions/mteam.ts (blob 8bd37832d18f08d7ff4901c8fcf6a758a1212bac)

Offline tests use synthetic responses and fake keys. No credentials, signed URLs, private torrent metadata, or account details are fixtures.

Web session (added 2026-11-03, verified with a real account; no real data kept in repository):
- Source: site frontend https://kp.m-team.cc (static.m-team.cc/static/js/main.*.js and route chunks)
- Signing (axios interceptor): body gets _timestamp=<ms> and _sgin=base64(HMAC-SHA1("POST&/api<path>&<ms>", "HLkPcWmycL57mfJt"));
  headers ts=<s>, visitorId=<client id>, version=2.0.0, webVersion=2000, authorization=<JWT>, did=<device id>
- POST /login: form {username,password,turnstile:""[,otpCode|emailCode|tgCode]}; code 0 → response headers authorization (JWT, ~30 days) and did;
  1001 → data lists verify methods (otp/email/tg); 1002 → account email must be verified in browser
- POST /member/sendLoginEmailVerifyCode: form {username,email}; only valid right after a /login that returned 1001
- POST /torrent/collection: form {id,make}
- POST /torrent/search: JSON with onlyFav=1 lists bookmarks
- POST /member/getUserTorrentList: JSON {userid,type:SEEDING|LEECHING|COMPLETED|INCOMPLETE|UPLOADED,pageNumber,pageSize}; rows {torrent,peer}
- POST /credit/logs: JSON {uid,pageNumber,pageSize,type:null}; rows {operation,bonus,uploaded,downloaded,text,createdDate,relatedId}
- POST /msg/search: form {box:1|-2|-1,keyword,pageNumber,pageSize}; POST /msg/read: form {msgId} (does not mark read; /msg/markRead is separate)
- Download: /torrent/genDlToken URL (api.m-team.cc/api/rss/dlv2) 302-redirects to https://fr1.halomt.com/...; real download verified
